      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4414235813": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Assured is on a mission to modernize insurance. Claims processing (i.e. should we pay this claim?), while often overlooked, is the foundation of the entire industry. It’s currently highly manual, involving phone calls, faxes, and gut instinct, costing tens of billions of dollars a year. We can do better.\nAt Assured, we provide large insurers with the software solutions they need to win in a modern, technology-driven world. From self-service claim-filing software to backend fraud detection, we’re the engine that powers claims processing for some of the largest insurers in the world.\nThe challenges we face are deep and diverse, from creating digital experiences that provide comfort and clarity to claimants at their most stressed and vulnerable to orchestrating large-scale ML-driven decision-making on billions of dollars of claims payments, life at Assured is dynamic, collaborative, and rewarding.\nAs a Staff Backend Engineer , you’ll build reliable backend systems that enable AI agents to handle complex insurance workflows safely and at scale.\nSome of the Problems You'll Solve:\n🤖 Develop autonomous agents that complete meaningful work.\nCreate AI agents that inspect data, resolve conflicting accounts, identify next steps, communicate with users, gather missing information, and suggest decisions across complex, ambiguous real-world workflows through the entire claims lifecycle.\n🎙️ Build real-time, conversational AI systems.\nDevelop multi-modal text and voice agents that maintain context, handle interruptions, route requests to specialized capabilities, and adapt dynamically rather than follow rigid scripts.\n🚗 Transform Unstructured Information Into Interactive Experiences.\nFrom car accident dynamics to nuances of water damage, transform narratives and complex data into intuitive inputs & visualizations that help end users describe the events, and back office teams evaluate what happened.\n⚖️ Make agentic AI reliable in regulated environments.\nDesign systems across coverage validation, liability determination, and beyond that give AI room to reason and adapt while deterministic controls guarantee compliance with legal, business, and safety requirements.\n📚 Process unstructured data at enterprise scale.\nBuild pipelines that ingest large volumes of audio, documents, images, and free-form text, then extract accurate, structured information for downstream systems.\n🕵️ Solve adversarial fraud and trust problems.\nDetect manipulated media, uncover behavioral patterns, resolve identities across disconnected datasets, and build systems that evolve as attackers change their methods.\n🏗️ Evolve key systems without disrupting production.\nRe-architect high-traffic systems through staged migrations, parallel processing, dual writes, and carefully coordinated evolution while preserving reliability and data integrity.\n🌐 Build shared services used across the entire product ecosystem.\nCreate reusable services and APIs to expose the work you do to both internal and external teams, as we modularize our capabilities to work across touchpoints and modes of engagement.\nHow You'll Make an Impact:\n🌎 Build important systems from start to finish.\nTurn product and business needs into reliable backend services, taking projects through development, testing, deployment, and ongoing improvement.\n🧩 Solve complex technical problems.\nWork through unclear requirements, evaluate tradeoffs, and find practical solutions that balance speed, quality, and maintainability.\n🔍 Help keep our production systems reliable.\nImprove testing, observability, automation, and operational practices so teams can ship confidently and respond quickly when problems arise.\n🤝 Support And Collaborate With Other Engineers.\nShare knowledge, provide thoughtful feedback, and work closely with engineering, product, infrastructure, and data teams to deliver successful projects.\n⚡ Use AI to work faster and more effectively.\nUse tools such as Claude, Codex, Cursor, and similar platforms to support development, debugging, testing, documentation, and operational work.\nYou'll Probably Thrive Here If You:\n🏗️ Have deep backend and systems expertise.\nYou bring 8+ years of backend or full-stack engineering experience, ideally within SaaS platforms or high-scale distributed systems environments.\n🛠️ Work with a modern backend and AI stack.\nOur stack includes TypeScript, Node.js, PostgreSQL, AWS, Kubernetes, GraphQL, and LLM tooling such as LangGraph, LangChain, and others. Experience with every tool isn’t required—we value strong engineering fundamentals and the ability to learn quickly.\n📈 Know how to scale systems through growth.\nYou have designed, scaled, and operated complex backend systems from early-stage growth through greater maturity.\n⚡ Balance rapid execution with durable engineering.\nYou move quickly while exercising the judgment needed to protect long-term reliability, scalability, and maintainability.\n💬 Lead through collaboration and pragmatism.\nYou work effectively across engineering, product, infrastructure, and data teams and can guide technical decisions without losing sight of business and customer needs.\n🔄 Adapt quickly to new tools and technologies.\nYour engineering judgment and ability to learn matter more than experience with a particular framework or language. Great engineers learn new technologies. Great systems thinking is harder to teach.\nBenefits:\n🤑 Competitive Compensation: Competitive salary and equity packages for all employees\n🏥 Healthcare Plan: Platinum medical, dental, and vision\n🛡️ Free life insurance: Including long-term disability & short-term disability\n🏄 Unlimited PTO: Uncapped vacation days & paid holidays\n👶 Family Leave: Maternity & paternity\n📈 401(k) Contribution: Assured contributes 3% of your income, even if you don't contribute\n🏠 WFH Benefits: Lunch on us 2x/week, monthly phone stipend & other home office perks\n👪 Health FSAs & HSAs: Pre-tax accounts for out-of-pocket medical expenses\n🤝 Team events & Offsites: We're remote, but we regularly get together\n**We have been made aware of individuals falsely posing as recruiters from Assured Insurance Technologies Inc. Please note that we only contact candidates from official @ assured.claims email addresses and all interviews are conducted through verified company channels. If you are unsure whether a message is legitimate, please contact us directly at recruiting-ops@assured.claims before sharing any personal information **\nOur Commitment:\nWe are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.\nCompensation Range: $210K - $270K",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4434146308": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Canonical is a leading provider of open source software and operating systems to the global enterprise and technology markets. Our platform, Ubuntu, is very widely used in breakthrough enterprise initiatives such as public cloud, data science, AI, engineering innovation, and IoT. Our customers include the world's leading public cloud and silicon providers, and industry leaders in many sectors. The company is a pioneer of global distributed collaboration, with 1200+ colleagues in 75+ countries and very few office-based roles. Teams meet two to four times yearly in person, in interesting locations around the world, to align on strategy and execution.\nThe company is founder-led, profitable, and growing.\nThis is an exciting opportunity for a software engineer passionate about open source software, Linux, Python, and web services at scale. We are building the next generation management solution for Ubuntu in the enterprise - on premise and on the public cloud - to enable large estate observability, telemetry, security, compliance and operations. Build a rewarding, meaningful career working with the best and brightest people in technology at Canonical, a growing international software company.\nLandscape is the leading management tool to deploy, monitor and manage fleets of Ubuntu systems, including package and repository management, health and security monitoring, hardware inventory, and automation. As Landscape software engineer you will be responsible for contributing on a distributed development team participating in all facets of the development process.\nLocation: This role will be based remotely in the Americas region.\nWhat you’ll do\nCollaborate proactively with a distributed team\nWrite high-quality code to create new features, fix bugs and modernize the Landscape codebase\nDemonstrate your strong commitment to code quality and automated testing\nParticipate in the engineering process with code and architectural reviews\nTake personal ownership of problems and design and deliver solutions\nWork remotely with global travel 2 to 4 weeks for internal and external events\nAssist with release management during each development cycle\nCollaborate with devops for Landscape SaaS, Canonical’s hosted Landscape\nWho you are\nYou love technology and working with brilliant people\nYou are curious, flexible, articulate, and accountable\nYou value soft skills and are passionate, enterprising, thoughtful, and self-motivated\nYou have a Bachelor’s or equivalent in Computer Science, STEM or similar degree\nYou have proficiency developing public-facing APIs and web applications, preferably using Python.\nExperience with Python and web frameworks such as Flask and Django.\nExperience with databases, and ORMs (PostgreSQL a plus)\nYou are comfortable with Ubuntu as a development and deployment platform.\nWhat we offer colleagues\nWe consider geographical location, experience, and performance in shaping compensation worldwide. We revisit compensation annually (and more often for graduates and associates) to ensure we recognize outstanding performance. In addition to base pay, we offer a performance-driven annual bonus or commission. We provide all team members with additional benefits which reflect our values and ideals. We balance our programs to meet local needs and ensure fairness globally.\nDistributed work environment with twice-yearly team sprints in person\nPersonal learning and development budget of USD 2,000 per year\nAnnual compensation review\nRecognition rewards\nAnnual holiday leave\nMaternity and paternity leave\nTeam Member Assistance Program & Wellness Platform\nOpportunity to travel to new locations to meet colleagues\nPriority Pass and travel upgrades for long-haul company events\nAbout Canonical\nCanonical is a pioneering tech firm at the forefront of the global move to open source. As the company that publishes Ubuntu, one of the most important open-source projects and the platform for AI, IoT, and the cloud, we are changing the world of software. We recruit on a global basis and set a very high standard for people joining the company. We expect excellence; in order to succeed, we need to be the best at what we do. Most colleagues at Canonical have worked from home since our inception in 2004. Working here is a step into the future and will challenge you to think differently, work smarter, learn new skills, and raise your game.\nCanonical is an equal opportunity employer\nWe are proud to foster a workplace free from discrimination. Diversity of experience, perspectives, and background create a better work environment and better products. Whatever your identity, we will give your application fair consideration.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485058457": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Description\nWe are seeking a technically strong Distributed Cache & Java Support Engineer to support distributed caching solutions and onboard Java and Spring Boot application use cases to the distributed-cache platform.\nThe candidate will combine hands-on Java development with practical enterprise distributed cache or in-memory data grid experience.\nThe role focuses on cache use-case assessment and onboarding, Java integration support, distributed-cache troubleshooting, and JVM diagnostics.\nKey Responsibilities\nProvide production support for distributed cache clusters and related Java application integrations\nMonitor cluster health, partition distribution, memory, latency, throughput, capacity, and performance\nSupport cache configuration and troubleshooting across distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction and expiry/TTL, partitioning, backup and replication, serialization, and cluster discovery\nDiagnose cache-related incidents including high latency, memory pressure, member restarts, split-brain conditions, data inconsistency, and degraded performance\nCoordinate with application, infrastructure, and vendor support teams to investigate issues and drive technical resolution\nReview and modify Java or Spring Boot code required to onboard application use cases to the distributed-cache platform\nWork with application teams to understand the use case, data model, access pattern, expected load, and caching objectives\nImplement application-side cache integration changes and validate serialization, distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction/TTL, and client configuration\nTroubleshoot JVM and application issues encountered during onboarding, integration testing, and production stabilization\nMinimum Qualification & Experience\nBachelor's degree in computer science, Software Engineering, or Information Technology\n7+ years of relevant experience in Java backend development, Java application support, distributed systems, or closely related engineering work\n3+ years of hands-on experience with distributed caching or in-memory data grid technologies in conjunction with Java applications\nMust Have\nStrong hands-on Java development experience, including the ability to write and modify Java code\nStrong JVM troubleshooting capability, including memory management, garbage collection, thread dumps, heap analysis, and performance diagnosis\nHands-on Spring Boot development or application-support experience, including cache integration or use-case onboarding\nHands-on experience with any distributed caching or in-memory data grid technology such as Redis, Hazelcast, Apache Ignite, Ehcache, Oracle Coherence, Infinispan, Memcached, or comparable platforms. Training will be provided on the selected platform.\nStrong understanding of distributed maps, Near Cache, eviction/expiry/TTL, partitioning, backup/replication, split-brain, serialization, and cluster discovery\nGood to Have\nProduction application support experience in banking, telecom, or other mission-critical environments, including incident triage, root cause analysis, and documentation\nBasic support-level exposure to Kubernetes, containers, Linux, networking, and optionally Anthos or OpenShift; deep platform expertise is not required\nFamiliarity with CI/CD processes and deployment-pipeline troubleshooting\nExperience with Splunk, AppDynamics, or Hazel cast Management Center, plus basic TLS/mTLS and certificate troubleshooting.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485064507": {
