        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis organization operates in the software engineering sector, focusing on developing internal tools, services, workflows, and AI-powered products that support engineering, operations, and recruiting platforms. It addresses the challenge of creating scalable, reliable software systems that enhance internal processes and productivity. The company is positioned to impact the engineering and operational efficiency through innovative platform capabilities.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER, NEW GRAD role is designed for recent graduates and early-career engineers aiming to accelerate their professional growth by building production software systems. This position involves contributing to and eventually owning core internal platform capabilities and product features. The role is critical in supporting internal workflows and platforms, ensuring the delivery of reliable, maintainable, and scalable software solutions.\nResponsibilities:\nContribute to the design and development of end-to-end fullstack systems supporting critical internal workflows and platforms.\nBuild maintainable backend services and APIs following scalable engineering practices.\nDevelop high-quality frontend interfaces for internal teams and end users.\nParticipate in data modeling and database optimization, including schema design and query performance.\nCollaborate with product, operations, and design teams to translate concepts into production-ready features.\nImprove engineering quality through code reviews, testing, documentation, and continuous improvements.\nAssist in troubleshooting production issues to build resilient and observable systems.\nDevelop engineering judgment to balance speed, scalability, and maintainability.\nRequirements:\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or related field (recent graduate or soon to graduate).\nExperience through internships, co-ops, research, or personal projects in software application development.\nStrong fundamentals in JavaScript and/or TypeScript.\nFamiliarity with frontend development using React or similar frameworks.\nFamiliarity with backend development using Node.js (NestJS is a plus).\nUnderstanding of relational databases such as PostgreSQL and data modeling principles.\nKnowledge of RESTful APIs and distributed application communication.\nExposure to Git and modern software development workflows.\nStrong problem-solving skills, curiosity, attention to detail, and a growth mindset.\nMotivation to learn quickly and contribute in a fast-paced engineering environment.\nPreferred:\nInternship or professional software engineering experience.\nExposure to cloud platforms like AWS, GCP, or Azure.\nFamiliarity with CI/CD, deployment pipelines, or DevOps fundamentals.\nExposure to modern architectures such as microservices, serverless, or event-driven systems.\nInterest in AI-powered products, workflow automation, or data-intensive applications.\nExperience contributing to team projects, hackathons, open-source software, or startup environments.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe pay range and compensation package for this role will be determined based on the candidate's experience, skills, and other relevant factors.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485074709": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "This is a Fully Remote Job\nAbout Our Client:\nThis organization operates in the digital fitness and entertainment space, focusing on creating engaging online platforms for cycling, running, and overall fitness communities. It addresses challenges in providing seamless and scalable web services that support user acquisition, subscription management, and e-commerce. The company is engaged in modernizing its web presence to enhance performance, accessibility, and integration with identity and commerce systems, aiming to grow its active community.\nAbout the Opportunity:\nThe SOFTWARE ENGINEER role involves rebuilding and enhancing the company’s web platform to improve customer acquisition, subscription management, and e-commerce experiences. The position requires collaboration within a cross-functional team to deliver reliable, high-performance features and establish a robust technical foundation. The role significantly contributes to the platform’s scalability, usability, and growth by addressing core customer journeys and operational efficiencies.\nResponsibilities:\nDevelop and maintain features across microservice backends, client platforms, e-commerce, and subscription systems.\nDesign and implement reusable, reliable, and high-performance code in various programming environments.\nEstablish and support web platform foundations including rendering, caching, CDN management, API patterns, CI/CD, observability, and legacy system decommissioning.\nCreate reusable page templates, content models, and CMS integrations to support marketing and content teams.\nCollaborate through code reviews, technical discussions, and pair programming.\nParticipate in on-call support and troubleshooting for team-owned services.\nIdentify technical risks and develop mitigation strategies.\nUtilize AI-assisted development tools responsibly to enhance development efficiency while maintaining quality standards.\nWork with engineers and product managers to scope and plan projects.\nContribute to the interview and hiring process.\nRequirements:\nBS or MS degree in Computer Science or related technical field.\n2 to 5 years of software development experience.\nStrong skills in modern JavaScript or TypeScript and component-based frontend frameworks such as React.\nProficiency in one or more development technologies, with preference for React, Java, or Kotlin.\nExperience in web development, frontend architecture, cloud microservices, or event sourcing.\nKnowledge of server-rendered or hybrid web frameworks; experience with Next.js is strongly preferred.\nUnderstanding of web performance, accessibility, analytics, and SEO fundamentals.\nFamiliarity with software engineering best practices including automated testing, monitoring, CI, and code reviews.\nExperience in production troubleshooting and on-call support.\nDemonstrated determination and eagerness to learn in a dynamic environment.\nPay Range and Compensation Package:\nThe base salary for this position ranges between $86,500.00 to $135,000.00, determined by role specifics, candidate qualifications, and location.\nThe compensation package includes performance bonuses, equity, and a comprehensive suite of medical, financial, and other benefits for eligible employees.\nEqual Opportunity Statement: Our client is an equal opportunity employer. They celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, or national origin.\nNote:\nTalentHop is a recruitment partner of this role. Please note that all employment decisions, including candidate assessment, interviews, hiring, compensation, and employment terms, are made exclusively by the hiring employer.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485080236": {
