        "payload": {
          "description": "Who WE are?\nKAVAK is the number one e-commerce in the purchase and sale of pre-owned vehicles with the fastest growth in Latin America. We work smart and make things happen, offering the easiest, safest and most transparent experience to buy or sell a car .\nBut our journey doesn't stop there: at KAVAK our goal is global! Now our footprint extends to the vibrant GCC region as part of our expansion into the Middle East, in the pursuit of our one and only goal: to transform the automotive market around the world.\nToday we have more than 180 Kavakees on the GCC team and growing, surrounding ourselves with the best talent to continue building the technology, processes, and products that make us the number one player in the pre-owned car market .\nWanna join us on this exciting ride?\nJob Description\nThis is a remote position open to candidates based anywhere in PAKISTAN ONLY .\nKey Responsibilities:\nYou’ll build our new ReactNative-app for iOS and Android, working closely with our team, who sets the architecture and technical direction. You’ll turn that design into a polished, production-ready app by building features end to end, writing tests and taking releases through the App Store and Google Play. It’s a hands-on, high-impact role where your work shapes how thousands of buyers bid on cars.\nRequirements\nSkills and Qualifications:\n5+ years of mobile development, including 3+ years with ReactNative and TypeScript.\nAt least two apps you've shipped to both the App Store and Google Play.\nExperience owning an app's full lifecycle, from setup to production support.\nWorking knowledge of iOS (Swift) and Android (Kotlin) for modules.\nExperience with real-time features (WebSockets or similar), push notifications and deep linking.\nStrong habits in testing, performance and mobile security.\nClear communication in English.\nDo you want to be part of this story? Apply now!",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485503259": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "About NETSOL: NETSOL Technologies is at the forefront of providing sophisticated software and services for asset financing and leasing. Our solutions cater to the automotive, equipment, banking, and lending industries with our comprehensive suite of IT services, including software development, AWS consulting, and more.\nAbout The Role\nWe at Netsol Cloud Services department are looking for a skilled React.js/Node.js Application Developer with at least one year of professional experience to join our development team. The ideal candidate will have a strong background in front-end and back-end development, with expertise in React.js and Node.js. Additionally, experience with AWS services is highly preferable.\nResponsibilities\nDevelop and maintain high-quality web applications using React.js for the front-end and Node.js for the back end.\nCollaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features.\nOptimize applications for maximum speed and scalability.\nImplement responsive designs and ensure compatibility across various devices and browsers.\nWrite clean, maintainable, and efficient code.\nTroubleshoot and debug applications to resolve issues and improve performance.\nStay up to date with the latest trends and technologies in web development.\nRequirements\nBachelor’s degree in computer science, Engineering, or a related field.\nMinimum of one year of professional experience as a React.js/Node.js Developer.\nProficient understanding of React.js and its core principles.\nExperience with popular React.js workflows (such as Redux, Flux, or Context API).\nSolid understanding of Node.js and its ecosystem.\nFamiliarity with server-side templating languages (e.g., EJS, Handlebars).\nKnowledge of AWS services (e.g., EC2, S3, Lambda) is highly preferable.\nExperience with front-end build tools (e.g., Webpack, Babel) and package managers (e.g., npm, Yarn).\nStrong understanding of RESTful APIs and asynchronous request handling.\nFamiliarity with version control systems (e.g., Git).\nExcellent problem-solving and communication skills.\nAbility to work independently as well as collaboratively in a team environment.\nAttention to detail and a passion for writing clean and efficient code.\nAPPLY HERE",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485584642": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Position: Freelance Computer Programmer – Code Review & System Optimization\nDepartment: Information Technology\nProject: DT Brain\nEmployment Type: Freelance / Project-Based\nReporting To: Chief Technology Officer (CTO)\nCompany: Dany Tameerat\nJob Overview\nDany Tameerat is seeking a skilled and experienced Freelance Computer Programmer to conduct a comprehensive technical review, optimization, and enhancement of DT Brain, the company's integrated business management system.\nDT Brain supports multiple business functions, including Sales CRM, Finance, Human Resources, Payroll, Project Management, Recruitment, and Executive Reporting.\nThe ideal candidate will possess strong programming expertise, with proven experience in reviewing existing codebases, identifying technical gaps, resolving performance and security issues, and implementing sustainable improvements to enhance overall system efficiency, reliability, and maintainability.\nKey Responsibilities\n1. Code Review & Technical Assessment\nConduct a comprehensive review of the existing application codebase.\nIdentify technical deficiencies, vulnerabilities, inefficiencies, and areas requiring improvement.\nProvide a prioritized assessment of recommended fixes and upgrades.\n2. System Performance & Optimization\nIdentify and resolve performance bottlenecks across application pages, database queries, and background processes.\nOptimize database queries, indexing, and overall application responsiveness.\nImprove system efficiency without disrupting existing business operations.\n3. Application Security & Reliability\nAssess authentication mechanisms, role-based access controls, data handling, and software dependencies.\nIdentify and address potential security vulnerabilities in accordance with established web application security practices.\nStrengthen system stability, reliability, and data protection.\n4. Code Quality & System Enhancement\nRefactor and restructure existing code to improve readability, scalability, and maintainability.\nImplement necessary technical upgrades while preserving existing system functionality.\nRecommend improvements aligned with long-term system requirements.\n5. Testing & Quality Assurance\nReview existing automated test coverage and ensure current test suites remain functional.\nDevelop additional tests where necessary to validate system improvements.\nIdentify and resolve defects introduced or discovered during the optimization process.\n6. Technical Documentation & Handover\nMaintain clear documentation of technical findings, modifications, and implemented improvements.\nSubmit a concise technical assessment and completion report.\nProvide recommendations for future system enhancements and maintenance.\nRequired Qualifications & Skills\nDemonstrated professional experience in software development, programming, and maintaining web-based applications.\nStrong proficiency in one or more programming languages, with the ability to understand and work with existing application architectures.\nPractical experience with Python, Flask, and Jinja-based applications , or demonstrable ability to work effectively with this technology stack.\nStrong understanding of relational databases, including SQLite or SQL-based systems, query optimization, and indexing.\nWorking knowledge of JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\nProven expertise in code auditing, debugging, refactoring, performance optimization, and technical troubleshooting.\nFamiliarity with automated testing frameworks, including pytest or equivalent tools.\nUnderstanding of web application security principles, authentication, authorization, and OWASP Top 10.\nStrong analytical, problem-solving, documentation, and communication skills.\nPreferred Qualifications\nPrevious experience working with ERP, CRM, finance, or enterprise business management applications.\nFamiliarity with Windows-based server environments and scheduled background processes.\nKnowledge of Node.js or additional web development technologies.\nExperience independently reviewing and upgrading existing business-critical applications.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4485826118": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Backend Software Engineer (Node.js / Full-Stack)\nVision71 Technologies | Karachi | Full-time, On-site\nABOUT THE ROLE\nVision71 Technologies builds practical software for business needs. We need a dependable engineer who can build, debug, test, document and deliver software. Backend development is the priority, with React/Next.js contributions when needed. You will work with our technical lead and a small team on client and internal projects.\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n• Build and maintain Node.js applications, REST APIs and integrations using JavaScript/TypeScript and Express, NestJS or similar frameworks.\n• Design data models and efficient queries using SQL and/or MongoDB according to project needs.\n• Implement authentication, authorization, validation, error handling and secure handling of credentials and business data.\n• Reproduce bugs, investigate logs, fix root causes and add appropriate automated tests.\n• Improve existing code, use Git branches and pull requests, and participate in code reviews.\n• Contribute to React/Next.js interfaces and connect them to backend services.\n• Support staging, approved deployments and production troubleshooting, with rollback planning and clear handovers.\n• Break requirements into tasks, estimate realistically and raise blockers and delivery risks early.\n• Maintain API documentation, setup instructions, task updates and handover notes.\n• Evaluate new tools through focused prototypes when there is a clear project need.\nREQUIREMENTS\n• Around 2–4 years of hands-on development experience preferred; strong candidates outside this range are welcome.\n• Practical Node.js and JavaScript/TypeScript skills, including asynchronous code, API design and debugging.\n• Experience delivering or maintaining an application used by real users; ability to explain your personal contribution.\n• Working knowledge of database design, queries, indexes and migrations appropriate to your stack.\n• Familiarity with React or Next.js, Git, API testing and automated testing.\n• Sound judgement about maintainability, security and technical trade-offs.\n• Clear communication and ability to work full-time on-site in Karachi.\n• Relevant degree or equivalent demonstrable practical experience.\nHELPFUL ADDITIONAL SKILLS\nDocker, Linux, CI/CD, cloud hosting, background jobs, queues, third-party APIs, reporting dashboards and business software integrations.\nINTEGRITY, RELIABILITY AND OWNERSHIP\n• Give accurate updates: distinguish implemented, tested, deployed and pending work. Never mark unfinished work complete.\n• Report mistakes, security concerns and likely delays promptly, with facts and a proposed next step.\n• Follow review and deployment approvals. Never hide a failed test or bypass safeguards to meet a deadline.\n• Respect confidentiality and intellectual property. Use only code, data and tools you are authorized to use.\n• Use AI tools responsibly, follow confidentiality rules, disclose material assistance in assessments and verify submitted code.\n• Honour agreed working hours and commitments, communicate availability changes promptly and maintain useful handovers.\nSUCCESS IN THIS ROLE\nUnderstand an existing codebase, deliver features with appropriate tests and documentation, communicate progress without repeated chasing and gradually own backend tasks from clarification to handover.\nHOW TO APPLY\nApply through LinkedIn with an accurate CV. Include portfolio or repository links in your CV if available, identifying work you personally completed. Do not share confidential code or credentials from previous employers.\nShortlisted applicants may explain a past project, complete a small role-relevant practical exercise and discuss debugging, delivery and accountability scenarios. Any reference checks will be discussed with you first. We value honest claims, clear reasoning and ownership. Candidates will be assessed on relevant skills, work evidence and role requirements. Expertise matters more than job titles. Compensation will be discussed based on demonstrated skills and role fit. Working hours and benefits will be clarified during the hiring process.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486054650": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "Job Overview:\nJoin our team as a Software Engineer and be at the forefront of creating innovative software solutions. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to design, develop, and maintain cutting-edge applications that drive our technological success. If you're passionate about coding, problem-solving, and contributing to impactful software, we welcome you to apply.\nJob Responsibilities:\nDesign, develop, test, maintain and improve the software.\nManage individual project priorities, deadlines and deliverables.\nDevelop high-quality, scalable, and interactive web applications.\nQualifications:\nBS degree in Computer Science or Software Engineering.\n02 - 04 years of experience in software development in Microsoft based, one or more general-purpose programming languages.\nExperience working the following technologies: web application development, HTML, CSS, JavaScript/JQuery, Angular, CVW, PWA, ASP.NET, SQL, WCF, Web APIs, Version Controlling, Application Security and CI/CD.\nExperienced in using tools including: Visual Studio, SQL Server, Team Foundation Server.\nIT healthcare domain knowledge will be preferable.\nO/A levels background will be preferred.\nDetailed knowledge of the IIS/Web server.\nInterest and ability to learn other coding languages as needed.\nWorking proficiency and communication skills in verbal and written English.\nCompensation & Benefits:\n💰 Financial:\nCompetitive salary and bi-annual bonus.\nFast track and uncapped career growth for high performers.\nCompany-sponsored vehicle financing (car and bike).\nInterest-free loans.\nProvident Fund: CureMD matches up to 8% of your base salary.\n🏥 Health and Wellness:\nIn-house clinic with a team of certified male and female doctors with 24/7 telemedicine service.\nHospital treatment monitoring by company doctors.\nComprehensive health coverage for your immediate family (outpatient, inpatient, maternity and parents' inpatient).\nExclusive health benefits and discounts at top class clinics and labs.\n🤝🏻 Supportive Workplace:\nPick-up and drop-off services for female employees.\nIn-house daycare facility.\nIn-house gym and recreational area to unwind.\n📚 Continued Learning:\nCompany-sponsored trainings, workshops, development programs and retreats.\nPaid specialized trainings/certifications.\nThe Difference You’ll Make:\nAt CureMD, every role, whether senior or junior, plays a pivotal part in transforming healthcare. By joining our innovative team, you’ll contribute to groundbreaking technology that directly impacts patient care, enhances healthcare efficiency, and saves lives globally. Your skills and passion will drive meaningful change, helping us deliver solutions that support healthcare professionals in critical, real-time settings. Together, we’re not just advancing technology — we’re making a tangible difference in people’s lives. Together, let’s save lives.",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486161894": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Zyte, we don't just collect web data—we solve complex web data challenges at scale. We are a globally distributed team that is bold, curious, and dedicated to building innovative ways to deliver clean, reliable web data from across the internet.\nData is our passion: We unlock access to open web data, empowering organizations—from startups to global enterprises—to power competitive intelligence, analytics, and AI pipelines\nRemote-first culture: Work from anywhere in the world. With over 260 Zytans across 33 countries, our strength comes from diverse backgrounds, perspectives, and skills\nEngineering excellence: We love diving deep into complex code bases, evaluating emerging technologies, and pushing technical boundaries. If you thrive on creative problem-solving and reliably delivering production-grade solutions, you will fit right in\nEstablished system design framework: We systematically analyze functional and product requirements alongside architectural trade-offs to make informed, sustainable design decisions\nReal-world distributed systems challenges: Tackle rare engineering problems in custom networking, high-throughput streaming, and large-scale orchestration under real-world operational constraints\nStrong product ownership: Work on a profitable, market-leading platform with dedicated time and resources allocated for architectural research and strategic feature engineering\nWhy This Role?\nZyte API fetches the web through a ladder of routes: plain HTTP, headless browsers, and, for the hardest targets, Edge—our own residential network of real devices. Edge is the tier that must succeed when everything else has failed. Today, a Rust peer on residential Windows PCs long-polls a single command-and-control service (CNC) over mTLS gRPC; CNC schedules fetches onto peers, runs a CONNECT proxy gateway, owns geo-routing, per-site cooldowns, and bandwidth quotas. It must grow from thousands of nodes to tens of millions of requests a day with rock-solid reliability.\nThe Edge Platform squad owns the control plane and data plane of this residential stack across Windows, Android, and Linux. The next step is building a proper Fleet Manager: a control plane with provider adapters (volunteer PCs, mobile-IP device farms, self-hosted nodes), a reconciler, rollout control, and metrics export sitting beside CNC as the data plane. You will design and operate that system—handling the scheduling, networking, proxying, and reliability work that turns residential devices into infrastructure other squads depend on. You will work directly with the Team Lead, a Principal Engineer, and partner engineering squads across Zyte.\nWhat You'll Do\nScale the data plane. Evolve CNC from a single-replica service into a horizontally scalable fetch scheduler: node selection that respects geo, site cooldowns, jail and per-peer quotas while avoiding detectable patterns, at 50-100M requests per day\nBuild the Fleet Manager control plane. Design and ship the inventory, health, configuration and software-rollout plane for the fleet: provider adapters, a reconciler, a rollout controller and an exporter to BigQuery, so a second device provider can be onboarded without bespoke scripts\nOwn the proxy path. Operate and improve the CONNECT proxy gateway and session handling on the edge, and work with the API squad on IP reputation, proxy leases and request scheduling so Edge slots cleanly into the platform's proxy plane\nEngineer the networking. mTLS gRPC between control plane and peers, long-poll and streaming semantics over unreliable residential links, NAT and carrier-grade NAT behaviour, and bandwidth accounting that is correct under contention\nMake it reliable. Define SLOs for availability, success and latency of the Edge route; build the metrics on peer count, drop-off and bandwidth that hold us and our supply partners accountable; run blue/green rollouts of CNC and peers safely\nShare production ownership. Take part in the squad's on-call rotation, lead incident post-mortems and turn operational lessons into platform improvements\nRaise the bar. Write RFDs for scheduling, fleet management and failover; review designs across the squad; and bring distributed-systems rigour (consistency, backpressure, idempotency, blast radius) to a young codebase\nRequirements\nWho You Are\n5+ years of production Rust experience, shipping and operating services you own end to end\nDistributed systems: you have designed and run schedulers, control planes or stateful services at scale, and can reason about consistency, partitions, backpressure and idempotency without a whiteboard\nDeep networking: TCP, TLS and HTTP at the handshake and packet level, gRPC and long-lived connections across NAT and lossy links, and what a client looks like on the wire\nProxy expertise: you have built or operated forward proxies, proxy gateways or residential/ISP proxy infrastructure, and understand IP reputation, session stickiness and pool health\nOps and reliability experience: SLOs and error budgets, observability you built yourself, production incidents you led, and comfort with being on call\nCross-platform awareness: comfortable with Rust running on Windows, Linux and Android targets, and with FFI boundaries when the data plane needs them\nAsync communication: strong written communication for a globally distributed, remote-first environment\nCurious problem solver: you like finding out why a system behaves the way it does under load, and fixing the cause rather than the symptom\nOur Tech Stack\nLanguages: Rust (tokio, tonic), C++ (Cronet) at the peer boundary; Python and Java in the services we integrate with\nProtocols: gRPC and protobuf over mTLS, HTTP CONNECT proxying, the Chromium network stack and our own browserless HTTP client\nInfrastructure: GCP and Kubernetes for the control plane, Terraform, blue/green deployments; multi-cloud (OCI, GCP) and data centres (Hetzner, Servers.com) across the wider platform\nData & Messaging: Valkey, BigQuery, Confluent Kafka\nMonitoring & Observability: Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, OpenTelemetry\nBonus Points\nMobile or desktop Rust: experience shipping Rust on Android, Windows or macOS, or binding Rust to C/C++ via FFI\nFleet or device management: reconcilers, rollout controllers, IoT or volunteer-computing fleets\nAnti-bot and fingerprinting: understanding of how TLS, HTTP and IP signals are used to classify traffic\nWeb scraping & crawling experience: familiarity with the technical challenges of large-scale web data extraction\nOpen source contributions: history of contributing to Rust, networking or distributed-systems open-source projects\nWhy Join Us?\nImpact at scale: Build the residential network tier behind web-scale data pipelines for top-tier global enterprises\nAutonomy and flexibility: Enjoy a genuine remote-first culture with flexible working hours and high organizational trust\nContinuous innovation: Solve emerging, complex technical challenges as AI and web data extraction rapidly evolve\nGlobal community: Collaborate with a passionate, diverse team of distributed systems engineers and data specialists across the world\nIf you are a Rust engineer who wants to turn tens of thousands of residential devices into dependable infrastructure, we would love to hear from you. Join us in building the fleet behind web data extraction at Zyte.\nBenefits\nBy joining the Zyte team, you will:\nBecome part of a self-motivated, progressive, multi-cultural team\nHave the freedom and flexibility to work from where you do your best work\nAttend conferences and meet with team members from across the globe\nWork with cutting-edge open source technologies and tools",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4486389351": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:12:45.732741+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "description": "At Precisely, we're not just building software — we're shaping the future of data integrity. As a global leader in data quality, data enrichment, and location intelligence, Precisely helps thousands of the world's most trusted brands make confident decisions with data they can rely on. We're an AI-first organization, which means artificial intelligence isn't a buzzword here — it's woven into how we build products, how we work, and how we think about solving complex problems for our customers. When you join Precisely, you join a team of curious, driven innovators who believe that better data makes the world run better. If you're ready to do meaningful work at the intersection of AI and data — and help define what's possible — we'd love for you to apply!\nOverview\nWe are seeking a passionate Associate Python Developer (AI) to join our engineering team building scalable Python applications. This opportunity is ideal for a candidate eager to learn, contribute, and grow in a collaborative, fast-paced environment. You will work under the guidance of experienced developers, participate in real projects, and develop your skills with modern Python tools and practices.\nWhat You Will Do\nAssist in designing, developing, and maintaining Python-based AI applications.\nWork with team members to understand requirements and implement features.\nLearn to use Pydantic for defining and validating data models.\nWrite clean, well-documented code with guidance.\nParticipate in code reviews and incorporate feedback.\nHelp troubleshoot and resolve basic technical issues.\nSupport testing and CI/CD processes.\nWhat We Are Looking For\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field, or similar.\nAt least 1 years experience building enterprise level software.\nGood knowledge of Python programming.\nExperience with TypeScript, JavaScript, or Node.js is a plus.\nEagerness to learn about the Python ecosystem, frameworks, and libraries.\nKnowledge of object-oriented programming and REST APIs.\nStrong problem-solving and communication skills.\nWillingness to take initiative and accept feedback.\nAbility to work effectively in a team and follow instructions.\nAI Skills/Knowledge\nKnowledge of large language models (LLMs) and AI coding harnesses such as Claude Code or GitHub Copilot.\nPreferred Skills (a Plus But Not Required)\nExposure to version control (Git) and testing concepts.\nExposure to backend development or data engineering concepts.\nFamiliarity with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, or Azure).\nThis position is 100% remote anywhere in the US\nApplication and Interview Impersonation Notice: Impersonating another individual when applying for employment, and/or participating in an interview process to assist another individual in obtaining employment, with Precisely Software Incorporated (“Precisely”) is unlawful. If Precisely identifies such fraudulent conduct, then as applicable and to the extent permitted by law, the application will be rejected, an offer (if made) will be rescinded, or the employment will be terminated, and legal action may be taken against the impersonators.\nThe personal data that you provide as a part of this job application will be handled in accordance with relevant laws. For more information about how Precisely handles the personal data of job applicants, please see the Precisely Candidate Privacy Notice",
          "source_url": ""
        }
      },
