      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/china-produces-about-85-of-the-worlds-cathode-share-7516513337908633600-8_eD": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:15:45.386040+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "China produces about 85% of the world's cathode active material. The West needs new battery chemistries to compete, but traditional R&D can take years to deliver them. \n \nToday, we announced $45M in funding to change that. \n \nBacked by  Zone II Ventures, and Course Corrected, we're scaling our AI-powered Discovery Engine, which combines 18 years of proprietary battery data with automated labs that physically build and test new materials. Over these 18 years our platform has run more than 225 projects for more than 85 customers across the battery value chain, including nearly a dozen Fortune 500 companies, and has resulted in more than 100 battery patents.  Along the way, the platform generated an internally consistent dataset covering more than 500,000 physical cells tested at over 165 million cycles.  \n \nOur technology has already helped deliver DRX, a new family of nickel- and cobalt-free cathode materials designed to reduce dependence on China. Now, we're bringing DRX toward commercialization while using AI to accelerate the next generation of breakthroughs. \n \nLed by founder and CEO Mathias Ingvarsson, COO and former Tesla manufacturing leader Steven Prast, and Chief Scientific Officer Dee Strand, we're building a faster path from battery discovery to commercial deployment. \n \nRead more in Fortune by Nick Lichtenberg. Article link in the first comment.",
          "posted_at": "2026-10-15T15:00:30.119Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/hira-wahid-437ab0267_we-are-hiring-position-nodejs-developer-activity-7464631549171347458-EXue": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:15:45.386040+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "🚀 We are Hiring!!!!\n\nPosition: Node.js Developer\nExperience: Fresh – 1 Year\n\n📍 Location: DHA Phase 2 Ext, Karachi.\n\nResponsibilities:\n\nDevelop and maintain backend applications using Node.js\nBuild and integrate REST APIs\nDebug and troubleshoot application issues\nCollaborate with development teams\nWork with databases and third-party integrations\n\nRequirements:\n\nBachelor’s degree in Computer Science or related field\nGood understanding of JavaScript and Node.js\nFamiliarity with Express.js and REST APIs\nBasic knowledge of MongoDB/MySQL\nUnderstanding of Git/version control is a plus\nGood problem-solving and communication skills\n\n📩 Interested candidates can share their resumes at hira.wahid@cee-solutions.com or hr@resourcelinked.tech with the position mentioned in the subject line",
          "posted_at": "2026-05-25T11:00:47.451Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/pakistan-it-jobs_hiring-backend-developer-nodejs-karachi-activity-7389224553194881024-m6qX": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:15:45.386040+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Hiring: Backend Developer (Node.js) – Karachi, Onsite\nWe’re looking for a passionate Backend Developer with strong expertise in Node.js to join our growing tech team in Karachi.\n\nWhat We’re Looking For:\n2+ years of hands-on experience with Node.js & Express.js\nStrong understanding of APIs, RESTful services & database design (MongoDB/MySQL)\nExperience with version control (Git)\nProblem-solving mindset & teamwork attitude\n\nWhat You’ll Do:\nBuild and maintain scalable backend systems\nCollaborate with frontend and mobile teams\nOptimize APIs for performance and security\n\n📍 Location: Karachi (Onsite)\n 🕒 Job Type: Full-time\nsend your cv at : hr@asoratech.com",
          "posted_at": "2025-10-29T09:00:18.607Z"
        }
      },
      "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/todd-simmons-55364412_north-carolina-at-students-march-back-to-ugcPost-7516656540976795649-Vavy": {
        "fetched_at": "2026-11-07T13:15:45.386040+00:00",
        "payload": {
          "status": "active",
          "text": "Clarification: On Thursday, Oct. 15, thousands of Aggie students took part in TWO major marches to downtown Greensboro:\n\n- The first was a March to the Polls, as previously described, which went from campus to the Union Square polling location downtown on the first day of early voting in North Carolina. Students marched back to campus after voting in protest of the Guilford County Elections Board's removal of their campus early voting polling location earlier this year.\n\n- The second was a March for Justice for Nolan Wells, the 18-year-old young man who tragically died July 4 under murky circumstances in the waters off Mississippi’s Horn Island after celebrating the Independence Day holiday. The march was organized by the A&T chapter of the NAACP, and a coalition of groups worked tirelessly to bring students together in solidarity for Nolan from across campus and the entire state. The march began at A&T’s February One monument, went downtown to the International Civil Rights Museum and returned to campus.\n\nIncredibly, thousands of Aggies took part in *both* marches, but in the video posted here, were returning from the second march, which concluded later. In both instances, outstanding civic leadership and participation were on full display from A&T students in the best tradition of Aggies, who have been leading in important community events since the university’s establishment in 1891. \n\nA&T continues to be America's largest HBCU, as well as its top-rated public HBCU in Forbes and US News & World Report.",
          "posted_at": ""
        }
      }
    },
    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T13:15:45.386040+00:00"
  },
